od of a vascular cause such as subclavian steal syndrome."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Has the patient experienced any recent head or neck trauma?", "Are there any symptoms of numbness or tingling in the face or legs?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["MRI of the brain", "Electromyography (EMG) of the right arm"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Vascular Causes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3, "posterior": 0.2608695652173913, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The combination of decreased sensation in the right arm, 2/5 strength in the right arm, and the patient's medical history of smoking and anabolic steroid use fits a neurological cause such as brachial plexopathy more than a vascular cause. Additionally, the patient's history of smoking 2 packs of cigarettes per day since age 25 and recent weight loss of 17 pounds may increase the likelihood of a vascular cause such as subclavian steal syndrome."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Has the patient experienced any recent chest pain or shortness of breath?", "Are there any symptoms of claudication in the legs?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Angiography of the subclavian artery", "Doppler ultrasound of the right arm"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Neoplastic Causes", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.1, "posterior": 0.07246376811594203, "danger": 0.4, 